		{"id":"551f6ee0c4cbd383","x":-620,"y":620,"width":921,"height":641,"type":"text","text":"layout_gen_design/              ← your Python project (create this folder)\n│\n├── src/                        ← all the Python code lives here\n│   ├── plot.py                 ← defines the site: a rectangle with width a and height b\n│   ├── group.py                ← defines one building group: a rectangle with a name\n│   ├── placer.py               ← places groups on the plot following the rules\n│   └── scorer.py               ← looks at a layout and gives it a score 0–100\n│\n├── dashboard/\n│   └── index.html              ← the web page where you see your layouts visually\n│\n├── data/\n│   └── buildings.xlsx          ← copy your Excel file here\n│\n├── outputs/                    ← when you run the program, images are saved here\n│\n└── main.py                     ← you run this: python main.py"},
		{"id":"4db1925fc20d2c19","x":-620,"y":-1120,"width":841,"height":700,"type":"text","text":"Layout_Gen_Design/              ← your Obsidian vault (already exists)\n│\n├── Canvas/\n│   └── overview.canvas         ← visual map of the whole project (drag & drop)\n│\n├── !Product_Vision.md           ← what is this project? what is the final goal?\n├── !Scoring_Logic.md            ← how do we score a layout? what makes it good?\n│\n├── Prototype/\n│   └── scratch.md               ← rough ideas, first sketches, nothing is final\n│\n├── Step_01/\n│   ├── Plan.md                  ← what exactly does Step 01 do? inputs, outputs\n│   ├── Group_PowerBlock.md      ← rules: \"place at center, surround with road...\"\n│   ├── Group_CoolingTower.md    ← rules: \"place on wind direction side...\"\n│   └── Group_GIS.md             ← rules: \"near Power Block transformers...\"\n│\n└── Step_02/\n    └── Plan.md                  ← empty for now — fill in later"}
